int MagicSum(Node * p) {
// Checking if the current node is a leaf node. If it is, then it cannot
be a Magic
Node since and hence
return 0;
if (!p→left && !p→right)
return 0;
int sum = 0;
// If the current node has 2 children and it is a magic node then add the
node' s value to the sum
if (p→left && p→right &&
(p→left→val % p→right→val == 0 || p→right→val % p→left→
val == 0))
sum += p→val;
// Recursively find MagicSum for left and right subtrees
3

if (p→left)
sum += MagicSum(p→left);
if (p→right)
sum += MagicSum(p→right);
return sum;
}
Second Question :
An M x N matrix (P) is present. The terms alternate between ‘X’ and ‘Y’. There will be a
list of queries. Each query is an array of size 3 ([a, b, c]). The first term represents the
query type. The next two term represent the index of element in the matrix. The first
query (a = 1) requires us to change the element at P[b][c] to ‘Y’. The second query (a = 2)
requires us to change the element at P[b][c] to ‘X’. The third query (a = 3) requires us to
print the matrix whose top left corner is P[b][c] and bottom right cornet is the end of the
matrix (i.e, P[M-1][N-1])
